WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
On almsround, Theravada monks
eat what they are given.

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.160
Sometimes that includes meat.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.860
Pali texts even show the
Buddha himself accepting pork,

4
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.210
offered as alms by a householder.

5
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.450
Yet the first precept is
to abstain from killing.

6
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.910
And one verse adds: nor cause slaughter.

7
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.720
So must a Buddhist be
vegetarian to avoid harm?

8
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.170
In this mission, you'll learn what ahimsa,

9
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.950
non-harming, asks of Buddhists,
towards animals as well as people.

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.080
Then you'll weigh four reasons
Buddhists give for why harm matters,

11
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.270
from karma to rebirth.

12
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: find out how Buddhists
answer the question of meat.
